  "mathematical_reason": "The actual thermal finite-state reward process has complete summable discounted returns and the stated safe cycle is genuinely the attained best value over every safe history. At gamma=4/5 its exact value is540/61. The unsafe route gives137/5-(4/5)p, so strict comparison is exactly p>5657/244. The real infinite-history optimum is attained; every optimal first action is safe iff this strict threshold holds for p>=0, and an unsafe globally maximizing history exists at equality. The literal decimal8.852459 is strictly below the exact safe value540/61, so putting that rounded number inside the strict threshold changes the exact threshold. The replacement preserves the actual exact rational before the existing six-decimal approximation; both safe-return/threshold rounding bounds, p24 strict separation and the higher gamma.8 threshold versus gamma.9 are genuine. This narrow review does not promote the entire exercise, other thermal material or the full40 family.",
